//! Raw WebSocket exchanges against the daemon, compared with what the pinned
//! original daemon sent for the same bytes
//! (`tests/fixtures/original-ws-vectors.json`, generated by
//! `gen-original-ws-vectors.cjs`): upgrade responses, close codes and reasons,
//! hello rejection, a second hello, receiver errors, and reconnect.
//!
//! Cases replay in the captured order against one daemon, as they ran against
//! the original, because a client id reused by a later case resumes the
//! earlier session. Client frames use an all-zero mask key. Server frames are
//! compared as opcode and exact payload. Allowed differences, none of them in
//! a close code, reason or frame order: the machine's host name in
//! `server_info`, and `features.workspaceLabels` (tracked gap DWLABEL-001).
//!
//! The session layer is a stand-in that accepts every schema-valid session
//! frame and delivers a protocol failure as the status/error frame the
//! original's session delivery sends, with the failure's text as its message.

mod common;

